**Diff summary**: Added `pull_request:` trigger, added an unconditional top-level `test` job (checkout → pnpm install → `pnpm test`), removed the `pnpm test` step from the `validate-okf` job, and added `if: github.event_name == 'push'` to `deploy`.

### (a) Missing/partial requirements
None of the acceptance criteria are missing structurally:
- "A pull request touching only TypeScript files runs the test suite" / "shell files does the same" — satisfied: `test` has no `needs`/`if`, so it runs on every `pull_request` and `push` regardless of which files changed.
- "The test job no longer depends on the markdown paths filter for its trigger" — satisfied: `test` job is independent of `check-changes`.
- "Markdown/MDX-only changes still run the OKF frontmatter validation they run today" — satisfied: `validate-okf` still gated by `needs.check-changes.outputs.markdown == 'true'`, unchanged except the `pnpm test` step was removed from it (now redundant since `test` runs separately).

### (b) Scope creep
> "A change that touches only TypeScript or shell files runs the test suite in CI" — the issue never mentions the `deploy` job.

The diff adds `if: github.event_name == 'push'` to `deploy`, which is not requested anywhere in the spec. This is arguably a *necessary* correction rather than pure creep — before this diff, `deploy` had no trigger guard at all, relying implicitly on the fact that only `push` events existed. Once `pull_request:` was added as a trigger, an unguarded `deploy` job would fire on every PR open/synchronize, attempting an S3/CloudFront deploy (and exposing `AWS_S3_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY`/`AWS_CF_DISTRIBUTION_ID` to PR context) — a serious regression. So while out-of-spec, it's a required side effect of the change and appears correctly done (guard restores prior push-to-main-only behavior; confirmed no double-deploy risk since `pull_request` default types opened/synchronize/reopened never include a merge-to-main `push`).

### (c) Implemented but questionable
- `deploy` still has no `needs:` on `test` (or `check-changes`/`validate-okf`). This is pre-existing (not introduced by this diff) but is now more conspicuous: on a push to `main`, a failing `pnpm test` in the new `test` job does **not** block `deploy` — it will still build and ship. The issue's stated motivation is "a failing test fails the check," which is true for the PR status check, but the deploy gate itself remains unguarded by test results. Not explicitly required by the spec, but worth flagging as a gap adjacent to this change's intent.
- `pull_request:` has no `types:` (defaults to opened/synchronize/reopened — fine) and no `branches:` filter, so `test`/`check-changes` now run for PRs targeting any base branch, not just `main`. Not called out as wrong by the spec, but a minor unstated scope widening.## Standards

