## Spec

**(a) Missing/partial requirements:** None. All four checkable acceptance criteria are satisfied — TS-only and shell-only PRs both run `test` (no `needs`/`if` gating it), `validate-okf` still runs on markdown/MDX via the unchanged `check-changes` filter, and `test` no longer depends on that filter. (The 5th criterion, verification against a real PR, is explicitly out of scope for this sandbox per the repair context.)

**(b) Scope creep:** Adding `if: github.event_name == 'push'` to `deploy` isn't asked for in the issue, but it's a necessary consequence of adding `pull_request:` as a trigger — without it, `deploy` would fire on every PR, running `pnpm build` and attempting an S3/CloudFront deploy with AWS secrets exposed to PR context. Correctly implemented, not a defect.

**(c) Implemented but questionable:** `deploy` still has no `needs: test`, so a failing test on a push to `main` doesn't block deployment — the check fails but the deploy proceeds anyway. This is pre-existing behavior (the old `validate-okf`-embedded test step didn't gate `deploy` either) and not something #65's acceptance criteria asked for, so it's not a regression introduced by this diff — worth a maintainer's awareness, not a blocking finding here. Also noted: `pull_request:` has no `branches:` filter, a minor unstated scope widening, not called out as wrong by the spec.

